<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21345] sanity test_807a: /mnt/lustre/d807a.sanity/single_dd expected blocks: 2048, got: 0</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21345</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;llsom_sync in one-shot mode discards the return value of lsom_start_update() and treats an empty changelog (EOF) as success, so it exits 0 and nothing is synced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the MDD changelog GC force-deregisters the user (space or catalog pressure), it also turns the changelog off and purges it. llsom_sync then reads 0 records, LSOM stays stale, and sanity test 807a fails with&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; "expected blocks: 2048, got: 0"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;even though the tool reported success.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
